# openapi-typescript declares `peerDependencies: { typescript: "^5.x" }` and has not published
# a release that admits TypeScript 7 — 7.13.0, the latest, still says ^5.x. This project is on
# TypeScript 7, so a strict peer resolution refuses to install.
#
# This is not new: the conflict exists in the repository today and was invisible only because a
# committed workspace lockfile is replayed by `npm ci` without re-resolving peers. Splitting the
# backend out surfaced it. Recorded here rather than papered over.
#
# The exposure is bounded. openapi-typescript is a devDependency that runs by hand
# (`npm run openapi:types`), its output is committed, and types are erased — nothing it produces
# reaches the runtime. Remove this line when upstream widens the peer range.
legacy-peer-deps=true
